; A paper edge is a segment bundle (ADR 0014), and incidence is checked in
; PAPER space (material identity), so `--cd & .c` names the unique boundary
; segment of the top edge whose paper preimage contains corner .c — the
; right half (1,1)-(0.5,1) — even though `fold --v` has stacked both halves
; onto the same table locus. (Before the paper-space incidence fix this
; wrongly reported "ambiguous: 2 segments match", checking table space where
; the folded halves coincide.)
paper square
fold --v = map .a onto .b
fold map --cd & .c onto --v

; assert steps = 2
; assert faces = 4
